  "synopsis": {
    "value": "Rib & Chop House is a Rocky Mountain-focused steak, seafood and ribs full-service concept founded by Burke and Melissa Moran in 2001 and operated by Finally Restaurant Group. The canonical pack lists 14 units, while current brand materials reference 13 locations, so the unit-count difference should remain visible rather than silently reconciled. For RBB, the CoS view is that the brand is a regional, centrally operated restaurant platform beginning to explore franchising. Technology strategy should emphasize full-service POS/payments, reservations and guest management, labor, kitchen execution, loyalty, reliability and measurable restaurant-level ROI, while watching whether franchise growth changes the buying model.",
